  "duration": 52.8,
  "vo": "Two hundred a month at twenty-five… or four hundred a month at thirty-five? [1-second silent pick] Same seven percent a year for both, until sixty-five. A puts in ninety-six grand. B puts in a hundred forty-four. Forty-eight grand more. Does B catch up? Age twenty-five: A starts. [1-second beat] At thirty-five: A’s got thirty-five grand. B: zero. Then B puts in double… and the gap… never… closes. Sixty-five. Who’s ahead, and by how much? Guess. [3-second pause] A. By about thirty-seven grand. With forty-eight grand less put in. Why? At thirty-five, A’s head start is thirty-five grand. That alone earns two-oh-two a month. B’s extra is two hundred. B never gains a dollar. Drop it to six percent, though, and B passes A at sixty-three and eight months. So: two hundred at twenty-five, or four hundred at thirty-five?",
  "captions": [
    {
      "t": 0.15,
      "end": 2.2,
      "text": "Two hundred a month at 25…"
    },
    {
      "t": 2.2,
      "end": 4.3,
      "text": "…or four hundred a month at 35?"
    },
    {
      "t": 5.6,
      "end": 8.6,
      "text": "Same 7% a year for both, until 65."
    },
    {
      "t": 8.6,
      "end": 12.2,
      "text": "A puts in 96 grand. B puts in 144."
    },
    {
      "t": 12.3,
      "end": 14.7,
      "text": "48 grand more. Does B catch up?"
    },
    {
      "t": 15.0,
      "end": 17.0,
      "text": "Age 25: A starts."
    },
    {
      "t": 18.0,
      "end": 20.7,
      "text": "At 35: A’s got 35 grand. B: zero."
    },
    {
      "t": 20.7,
      "end": 22.6,
      "text": "Then B puts in double…"
    },
    {
      "t": 22.6,
      "end": 25.4,
      "text": "…and the gap never closes."
    },
    {
      "t": 25.9,
      "end": 28.6,
      "text": "65. Who’s ahead, and by how much? Guess."
    },
    {
      "t": 31.6,
      "end": 35.4,
      "text": "A. By about 37 grand. With 48 grand less put in."
    },
    {
      "t": 35.8,
      "end": 39.1,
      "text": "Why? At 35, A’s head start is 35 grand."
    },
    {
      "t": 39.1,
      "end": 41.6,
      "text": "That alone earns $202 a month."
    },
    {
      "t": 41.6,
      "end": 44.4,
      "text": "B’s extra is $200. B never gains a dollar."
    },
    {
      "t": 44.5,
      "end": 49.0,
      "text": "Drop it to 6%, though, and B passes A at 63 and 8 months."
    },
    {
      "t": 49.35,
      "end": 52.6,
      "text": "So: $200 at 25, or $400 at 35?"
    }
